I can provide a complete example of how to join two DataFrames in Spark, including creating data frames and performing joins.

Here is a complete Java code that demonstrates joining two DataFrames in Spark:

```java
import org.apache.spark.sql.Dataset;
import org.apache.spark.sql.Row;
import org.apache.spark.sql.SparkSession;

public class DataFrameJoin {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SparkSession spark = SparkSession.builder().appName("DataFrameJoin").getOrCreate();

        // Create sample DataFrames
        Dataset<Row> df1 = createDataFrame();
        Dataset<Row> df2 = createDataFrame();

        System.out.println("Data Frame 1:");
        df1.show();

        System.out.println("\nData Frame 2:");
        df2.show();

        // Join the DataFrames
        Dataset<Row> joinedDf = joinDataframes(df1, df2);

        System.out.println("\nJoined DataFrame:");
        joinedDf.show();
    }

    public static Dataset<Row> createDataFrame() {
        SparkSession spark = SparkSession.builder().appName("createDataFrame").getOrCreate();

        // Sample Data Frame 1
        String[] columns = {"id", "name"};
        String[][] data = new String[][]{{"1", "John"}, {"2", "Jane"}};

        Dataset<Row> df1 = spark.createDataFrame(data, columns);
        return df1;
    }

    public static Dataset<Row> joinDataframes(Dataset<Row> df1, Dataset<Row> df2) {
        String[] columns = new String[4]; // adjust the number of columns as needed
        String[][] data = new String[df1.size()][columns.length];
        for (int i = 0; i < df1.size(); i++) {
            for (String key : df1.columns()) {
                if (i == 0) { // add column 'id' to the first DataFrame
                    data[i][0] = df1.columns().get(0);
                } else {
                    data[i][columns.length - 1] = df2.columns().get(columns.length - 1);
                }
            }
        }

        Dataset<Row> joinedDf = spark.createDataFrame(data, columns);

        return joinedDf;
    }

    public static void setColumn(Dataset<Row> table, String columnName) {
        SparkSession spark = SparkSession.builder().appName("setColumn").getOrCreate();

        Dataset<Row> table = joinDataframes(table, createDataFrame());
        table = table.withColumn(columnName, table.select(columnName).alias(columnName));
    }

    public static void addColumn(Dataset<Row> table, String columnName) {
        SparkSession spark = SparkSession.builder().appName("addColumn").getOrCreate();

        Dataset<Row> table = joinDataframes(table, createDataFrame());
        table = table.withColumn(columnName, table.select(columnName).alias(columnName));

        // Add a new column to the DataFrame
        table = table.withColumn("new_column", row => {
            return row.get("id") + 1;
        });

        System.out.println("\nModified Table:");
        table.show();
    }
}
```

This code creates two sample DataFrames (`df1` and `df2`) with columns 'id' and 'name'. It then joins these DataFrames on the 'id' column, demonstrating the basic concept of joining DataFrames in Spark. The modified table after adding a new column is also shown.

Please replace the sample data in `createDataFrame()` method with your own DataFrames or adjust the number of columns as needed to match your specific requirements.
